From 20ac4bab5506b5ab836d5b6e688653f3ef5487e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:26:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the colour format of the user is looked at
 only for a request that sets a mode

FlipPage() calls StageOutputFormat() with each frame. On an output that
has the colour format property (amdgpu with Linux 7.3, every HDMI and
DisplayPort connector; NVIDIA 620), it read the setting, looked up the
values of the property by name and built the key of the mode
("3840x2160@594000:0", several strings) for each frame of the menus and
of every video, and then OUTPUT_FORMAT::Stage() staged nothing unless the
request set a mode and native output did not have the output.

Those two are asked first now; for the other frames nothing else is done.
What is staged is the same. (A choice that the driver has no value for is
said in the log with the first mode set, instead of with the first
frame.) A check of the source (the window system is not built on the
host) fails without this and passes with it.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
index e14c74c..7e362fa 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
@@ -4802,7 +4802,12 @@ void CWinSystemGbm::StageOutputFormat()
   if (!m_outputFormatChoice)
     return;
   auto drm = std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDRMAtomic>(m_DRM);
-  CDRMConnector* connector = drm ? drm->GetConnector() : nullptr;
+  // (this is asked with each frame: only a request with a mode set takes the colour format, and
+  // not while native output owns it, OUTPUT_FORMAT::Stage(); nothing of the settings or of the
+  // mode is looked at for the others)
+  if (!drm || !drm->ModesetPending() || NativeDVOutputInUse())
+    return;
+  CDRMConnector* connector = drm->GetConnector();
   const auto component = CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent();
   const auto settings = component ? component->GetSettings() : nullptr;
   if (!connector || !settings)
